' @fileoverview Home screen section slot count.
'
' How many `homesectionN` slots JellyRock reads from the Jellyfin server's
' DisplayPreferences CustomPrefs. Mirrors MAX_SECTIONS in the Jellyfin web client
' (jellyfin-web, src/components/homesections/homesections.js), which has stored ten
' slots since server 10.10.0. The server itself does not cap the count, so this
' number follows the web client, not an API.
'
' Slots are numbered 0 to SLOT_COUNT - 1. Every slot needs a matching
' `homeSection<N>` field in components/data/jellyfin/JellyfinUserSettings.xml,
' because user.settings.Save() refuses a name the node does not declare. The
' HomeSlots spec fails if the two ever disagree.

namespace homeSlots

  const SLOT_COUNT = 10

end namespace
